次要终点:
Progression Free Survival

Clinical anti-tumor effect by standard criteria (RECIST v 1.1)

Complete response will be defined as the disappearance of all target lesions. All lymph nodes mustbe less than 10mm in short axis.

Partial response will be defined as a 30% decrease in the sum of the diameters of the target lesions. Stable disease will be defined as a change in sum of the diameters that does not meet criteria for progressive disease or partial response.

Progressive disease will be defined as either:

* An increase in the sum of diameters of target lesions of at least 20%;
* The comparison will be made to the smallest sum while the patient was on study;
* The absolute increase must be at least 5mm or;
* The appearance of new target lesion(s).

