5. Patients with prior or concurrent occurrence of other malignancies, with the following exceptions: a) Carcinoma in situ of the cervix or breast, curatively treated with no signs of recurrence for at least 3 years prior to the study; b) The primary malignancy was completely resected and in complete remission for ≥ 5 years;
